            "livingItOut": "To live out this verse today, think about the relationships in your life. Are there people you haven’t connected with in a while? Instead of just sending a text or an email, consider picking up the phone or meeting them in person. For example, if you have a friend or family member who is going through a tough time, a simple visit or a heartfelt conversation can mean so much more than just a written message. Make a plan this week to reach out and have a genuine conversation with someone you care about. This can strengthen your bond and make both of you feel more valued.",
            "godsLove": "This verse reminds us of how God desires a personal relationship with us. Just like John wants to connect with his friends in a deeper way, God wants to connect with us beyond just words on a page. He cares about our hearts and our struggles, and He longs to have direct conversations with us through prayer and worship. God's love is about intimacy and connection, showing us that He is always there, ready to listen and respond. When we take the time to talk to Him, we experience His care and guidance in our everyday lives, reassuring us that we are never alone.",
